{title: Aura Lee}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
As the [C]blackbird in the [G]spring, 'neath the [C]willow [F]tree,
Sat and [C]piped, I heard him [G7]sing, sing of [C]Aura [C]Lee.

{c: Chorus}
[F]Aura Lee, [C]Aura Lee, [D7]maid of golden [G7]hair,
[C]Sunshine [G7]came along with [C]thee, and [F]swallows [G7]in the [C]air.

{c: Verse 2}
In her [C]blush the rose was [G]born, 'twas [C]music when she [F]spake,
In her [C]eyes the light of [G7]morn sparkling [C]seemed to [C]break.
